  "title": "DSTDEV, DSTDEVP, DVAR, and DVARP compute variance via raw x87 PC64-stored moments with centered fallback, returning #DIV/0! on <2 (sample) or 0 (population) numbers",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0.20527, DSTDEV, DSTDEVP, DVAR, and DVARP collect numbers in matching records' field cells (ignoring text, logicals, and blanks while propagating errors), reject non-reference database arguments at formula entry (0x800A03EC), return #DIV/0! on 0 matching numbers (and on 1 matching number for sample DSTDEV/DVAR, whereas population DSTDEVP/DVARP return 0), and evaluate variance through Excel's x87 PC64-stored raw-moment sequence (switching to centered deviations when square_total / count / squares > 0.99, variance * 1000 <= |mean|, or non-finite, with staged sqrt for DSTDEV/DSTDEVP). All 6,507 DSTDEV, 5,673 DSTDEVP, 5,669 DVAR, and 5,670 DVARP full-bank rows match.",
